Z||000007||G-Nasty||02-09-2001||12:28 AM||||Check for a crack in the outer plastic assembly at the stalk. Mine did the same thing-use the turn signal and the wipers came on: Good luck on the excorsism... ||||reg||1
Z||000008||gabriel||02-09-2001||01:01 PM||||Yeah, I was thinking stalk cracks too, until today.  Turned on the headlights - turn signal comes on..  Turned OFF the fan - yep, turn signal came on!  Now I'm wondering if there is some common point where, if there is a problem, any electrical circut could short into the signal circut, thus causing a transitory activation. I mean, I never have to turn OFF the d**m thing. It just sweeps once & stops. All of the lettering on the fusebox is gone - doesn't help any, either.<P>Ah well, I could always solve the problem by disconnecting the wipers! LOL<BR>  Sees hours & hours of tedious work ahead .... sigh||||reg||1
